Fillets: a rounding whose ball rolls on a straight edge of the face beyond
a narrow top, the edge ending on the faces at the ends of the spine, rolls
on along the edge's line past its ends and is cut by those faces
(mitcad#236).

The case: an ear on the side of a cylindrical boss, its top a strip
narrower than the radius between the boss and a chamfer on the ear's outer
edge, the top's edge with the boss rounded. The ball touches the boss and
rolls on the top's edge with the chamfer (Er, a line), whose ends A lie on
the ear's sides; each side W also holds the spine's end vertex. Past Er's
ends OCCT turned the ball about A and rolled it on along W's edge with the
top, and the corners failed ("no point on arc", or at an end of more than
three edges "Failed to find edge"), or the result was invalid. The bodies
stored in the .f3d files roll the ball on along Er's line up to the
spine's ends and cut the blend there with W, from A to the boss's
contact; W grows up to the cut, its edge with the boss prolonged to the
contact (from the end vertex, where W and the boss meet at that vertex
only).

- ChFi3d_Builder::RolledOnProlongedEdge, called by PerformSetOfSurf: a
  SurfData P rolling on a straight edge Er of its face B from one end of
  Er to the other, each end on a face holding the spine's end vertex
  there, the stripe going on past Er's ends: the blend is walked again
  from the middle of P, both ways up to the guide's ends, rolling on Er's
  line as the edge of a strip of B's surface beside it on B's side (so
  that the ball still leaves the edge for B where it reaches into it), the
  other face's surface grown (a periodic one's seam half a period away),
  and replaces the stripe's SurfData; its end points lie on no edge.
- PerformOneCorner: at such an end (ChFi3d_RolledPastEdgeVertex: the
  contact on Er's side passes Er's vertex A, which lies on a face W
  holding the corner's vertex) the corner is an OnSame end with W the face
  at the end, the cap starting at A (on B's edge with W, the contact ending
  there), the face across Er consumed; W's edge with the opposite face at
  the vertex is prolonged as at any OnSame end. Where W and the opposite
  face meet at the vertex only (another face between them there), their
  intersection from the vertex to the opposite contact's end is a new edge
  of both (ChFi3d_CurveFromVertexToContact).
- PerformFilletOnVertex: such an end at a vertex of more than three edges
  is built that way (PerformRolledPastEnd) instead of by
  PerformIntersectionAtEnd.
- IntersUpdateOnSame: no prolonged edge, no tangent-face retry.

Upstream: new.
